# Native Kodak i2000 backend.
#
# The IDs are preserved from the vendor package.  The backend uses only
# sanei_usb and does not load the vendor TWAIN/OpenUSB stack.
#
# True physical-cold startup needs the volatile firmware images embedded in
# the exact Kodak i2000 v4.14 devicemanager container.  The file is parsed as
# data, never executed, and every required i2400 resource is size- and
# SHA-256-checked.  Persistent booter/flash updates are never performed.  This
# volatile path is live-verified on the i2400.  Prefer a compact bundle made
# once from a locally obtained vendor container:
# kodak-i2000-fw extract /opt/kodak/kds_i2000/lib/devicemanager.so \
#     /var/lib/sane/i2400-v4.14.kfw
# Uncomment only when cold-start recovery is required; warm scanners do not
# read or stage the bundle.  The original devicemanager.so is also accepted.
# firmware-source /var/lib/sane/i2400-v4.14.kfw
usb 0x040a 0x601c
usb 0x29cc 0x100a
usb 0x040a 0x601d
usb 0x29cc 0x100b
usb 0x040a 0x601e
usb 0x29cc 0x100c
